Hey everyone, say hello to Aki the female barbarian, my Second Best
Character Ever!  Why second best, you ask?  Because the best always
gets killed off by the RNG in the messiest way possible after I make
one of these posts.  Now listen up, Mr RNG: my Best Character Ever is
Terry the elven ranger.  He's sitting on level 1 wearing his kick-ass
+0 leather armour, waiting for you.  Go get him ;)

I only just started up Aki this morning, and already she shows a lot
of promise.  She went down to Minetown as soon as she found the down
stairs to the Mines and was looking so buff I decided to let her do
Mine's End before Sokoban.  One the way down she tamed a little dog
and had it eat a chameleon corpse.

"The little dog eats a chameleon corpse.  The little dog turns into an
arch-lich." <insert sound of me choking>

Now...is it safe for Aki to keep Bubbles around?  I know she doesn't
stand a chance of beating him if he turns feral...but *will* he turn
feral?  She's *very* careful around him and takes him everywhere, even
Sokoban.  The only way I can see of him becoming un-tame is if Aki or
Bubbles steps on a level teleporter and become separated for an
extended period of time.  But liches are uneating, and according to
the spoilers pets will only become hostile if they would have starved
to death in the time you were away.  But uneating pets...can't starve.
 So why is everyone so terrified of their pet archons turning against
them? (archons are also uneating) Is there some other way to piss them
off that I've missed?  Should I just ditch Bubbles in a nice, safe
place? (I know I'll lose him eventually anyway, since I plan on
genociding L)  He's pretty useful to have around right now though...

Well, Aki herself isn't particularly wussy either.  She took down a
vampire lord all by herself in Mine's End (after both her pets got
themselves frozen by a floating eye) and later killed a mumak in one
move.  Going back up to Minetown, she watched with a combination of
horror and glee as Bubbles killed every person there except the
priest, who he couldn't damage for some reason. (Everyone includes,
unfortunately, Izchak.  Aki buried his possessions just outside the
temple and engraved an epitaph above it with her wand of lightning.)

Aki bought a few points of protection with the shopkeepers' money,
then killed the priest (she had shock resistance, so it wasn't too big
a deal).  She emptied two wands of create monster and a bag of tricks
into the altar and ended up with Mjollnir, Werebane and several
potions of holy water.

Okay question time.  Despite being orcish, Aki got the "You murderer!"
message and lost telepathy upon killing the priest.  I always though
the priest and watchmen were supposed to be human - or are they
actually the race you are?  Why are the watchmen chaotic, anyway?  I
always think of them as lawful.  And why couldn't Bubbles attack the
priest when he mowed down guards in a matter of seconds?  Did it have
anything to do with being inside the temple?

About werebane: I figure if I don't sac for any more artifacts then I
have a pretty good chance of getting Grayswandir when I reach the
Castle <hopeful look>.  But if I don't for some reason will Werebane's
silver damage in Gehennom <VERY hopeful look> make up for its wimpy
attack? (I'm thinking no)  What weapons are good for a B?

Oh, and isn't Sokoban supposed to be a no-teleport zone?  Bubbles
didn't seem to have any trouble hopping around the place. (It's not
because he's faster than Aki - there were lots of times when she was
standing next to a pit without moving and he ended up falling down and
the only way that could have happened is if he'd 'ported onto one.)

